      ******************************************************************
      *  Testsuite : COCRDSLC CARD DETAIL VIEW TRANSACTION
      *  Program-under-test : app/cbl/COCRDSLC.cbl
      *
      *  Exercises COCRDSLC's card-detail-view CICS transaction by
      *  mocking ONLY the CICS-API boundary (CALL 'DFHEI1').  Internal
      *  paragraphs are NEVER mocked; every TESTCASE PERFORMs a
      *  production paragraph LIVE per AAP Section 0.10.1.
      *
      *  COCRDSLC is the simplest CICS card-read pattern: READ-ONLY
      *  with no WRITE/REWRITE/DELETE.  RECEIVE MAP -> 2210/2220
      *  edit -> 9100/9150 READ CARDDAT/CARDAIX -> SEND MAP.
      *
      *  Test categories (5 testcases, off-platform-reachable subset)
      *  -----------------------------------------------------------
      *    TC1 - 2220-EDIT-CARD accepts 16-digit number (L716-718)
      *    TC2 - 2220-EDIT-CARD rejects empty CC-CARD-NUM (L691-702)
      *    TC3 - 2220-EDIT-CARD rejects non-numeric (L706-715)
      *    TC4 - 2210-EDIT-ACCOUNT accepts 11-digit id (L675-678)
      *    TC5 - 1100-SCREEN-INIT populates CCRDSLAO headers
      *
      *  Test user: USER0001 (AAP 0.10.2).  AAP TC1/TC2/TC4/TC5 (full
      *  read / NOTFND / PF3 / XCTL) deferred to MOCK CICS support
      *  (DFHRESP undefined off-platform).
      *  References: AAP 0.10.1, 0.5.1, 0.10.2, 0.4.1, 0.7.1;
      *  app/cbl/COCRDSLC.cbl L247-410, L412-455, L596-723, L736-878;
      *  app/cpy/{COCOM01Y, CVCRD01Y, CVACT02Y}.cpy; cpy-bms/COCRDSL;
      *  tests/stubs/{STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy, DFHEI1.cbl};
      *  tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/CARD-FIXTURE-001.cpy;
      *  tests/cobol-check/{COSGN00C, COACTVWC, COTRN01C}.cut.
      *
      *  DFHEI1 fail-loudly safety net (QA CP4 Phase 5.2 anchor).
      *  Runner-script Step 5 injects EXTERNAL field declarations
      *  into merged WS; BEFORE-EACH resets WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-
      *  CALLED for per-testcase isolation of the safety-net flag.
      ******************************************************************
       COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG.

       TESTSUITE 'COCRDSLC CARD DETAIL VIEW TRANSACTION'.

      ******************************************************************
      *  BEFORE-EACH -- per-testcase isolation reset.
      *
      *  Restores deterministic baseline state so every TESTCASE
      *  starts from a known, identical configuration.  cobol-check
      *  resets MOCK invocation counters automatically between
      *  TESTCASEs; this block resets the production WS / shared
      *  structures touched by COCRDSLC:
      *
      *    WS-MISC-STORAGE     COCRDSLC.cbl lines 36-121; clears
      *                        WS-RESP-CD, WS-REAS-CD, WS-TRANID,
      *                        WS-INPUT-FLAG, WS-EDIT-ACCT-FLAG,
      *                        WS-EDIT-CARD-FLAG, WS-RETURN-FLAG,
      *                        WS-PFK-FLAG, CICS-OUTPUT-EDIT-VARS,
      *                        WS-CARD-RID, WS-FILE-ERROR-MESSAGE,
      *                        WS-LONG-MSG, WS-INFO-MSG, WS-RETURN-MSG
      *                        (matching 88-level WS-RETURN-MSG-OFF
      *                        on the LOW-VALUES VALUE per line 135).
      *    CC-WORK-AREAS       CVCRD01Y; clears CCARD-AID, CC-
      *                        ACCT-ID, CC-CARD-NUM, CC-CUST-ID and
      *                        the CCARD-NEXT-* / CCARD-ERROR-MSG
      *                        slots used by 1xxx/2xxx paragraphs.
      *    CARDDEMO-COMMAREA   COCOM01Y; clears CDEMO-FROM-* /
      *                        CDEMO-TO-* / CDEMO-USER-ID / CDEMO-
      *                        USER-TYPE / CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT /
      *                        CDEMO-ACCT-ID / CDEMO-CARD-NUM
      *                        (matches 88-level CDEMO-PGM-ENTER
      *                        with VALUE 0 on CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT).
      *    WS-THIS-PROGCOMMAREA  COCRDSLC.cbl lines 200-203; clears
      *                        CA-FROM-PROGRAM / CA-FROM-TRANID.
      *    CARD-RECORD         CVACT02Y 150-byte group; cleared for
      *                        forward-compatibility with the COPY
      *                        CARD-FIXTURE-001 post-translator
      *                        extension on 9100-GETCARD-BYACCTCARD.
      *    CCRDSLAI            BMS input map (cpy-bms/COCRDSL.CPY).
      *                        CCRDSLAO REDEFINES CCRDSLAI in the
      *                        production copybook so this also
      *                        clears CCRDSLAO.
      *    WS-CURDATE-DATA     CSDAT01Y date-time group used by
      *                        1100-SCREEN-INIT for header dates.
      *    RETURN-CODE         Implicit special-register reset.
      *
      *  After clearing, BEFORE-EACH seeds the COMMAREA with the
      *  USER0001 regular-user identity per AAP Section 0.10.2.
      *  CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM defaults to 'COMEN01C' / CDEMO-FROM-
      *  TRANID = 'CM00' to reflect the upstream caller (the main
      *  menu's option-4 dispatch -- COCRDSLC's most common entry
      *  pathway).  TC4's 2210-EDIT-ACCOUNT testcase overrides
      *  CC-ACCT-ID for the validation drive; TC1-TC3 leave the
      *  USER0001 default unchanged because 2220-EDIT-CARD is
      *  invariant to the COMMAREA's user identity.
      ******************************************************************
       BEFORE-EACH
            INITIALIZE WS-MISC-STORAGE
            INITIALIZE CC-WORK-AREAS
            INITIALIZE CARDDEMO-COMMAREA
            INITIALIZE WS-THIS-PROGCOMMAREA
            INITIALIZE CARD-RECORD
            INITIALIZE CCRDSLAI
            INITIALIZE WS-CURDATE-DATA
            MOVE ZERO       TO RETURN-CODE
            MOVE 'N'        TO WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED
            MOVE 'USER0001' TO CDEMO-USER-ID
            MOVE 'U'        TO CDEMO-USER-TYPE
            MOVE 'COMEN01C' TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM
            MOVE 'CM00'     TO CDEMO-FROM-TRANID
       END-BEFORE.


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC1 -- 2220-EDIT-CARD accepts a valid 16-digit card number
      *
      *  Drives 2220-EDIT-CARD (production lines 685-723) along the
      *  SUCCESS path that gates 9100-GETCARD-BYACCTCARD downstream.
      *  The paragraph executes:
      *
      *    SET FLG-CARDFILTER-NOT-OK TO TRUE              (line 688)
      *    IF CC-CARD-NUM = LOW-VALUES OR SPACES OR
      *       CC-CARD-NUM-N EQUAL ZEROS                   (line 691-3)
      *        ... (FALSE; '0000000000000001' is non-zero)
      *    IF CC-CARD-NUM IS NOT NUMERIC                  (line 706)
      *        ... (FALSE; '0000000000000001' is all-numeric)
      *    ELSE                                           (line 716)
      *        MOVE CC-CARD-NUM-N TO CDEMO-CARD-NUM       (line 717)
      *        SET FLG-CARDFILTER-ISVALID TO TRUE         (line 718)
      *    END-IF.
      *
      *  This is the off-platform expression of the AAP TC1 "Valid
      *  card number returns detail" pathway: production logic
      *  invariant that 9100-GETCARD-BYACCTCARD (production line
      *  344-345 via 9000-READ-DATA on lines 728-730) ONLY runs
      *  after BOTH 2210-EDIT-ACCOUNT and 2220-EDIT-CARD validate
      *  their respective inputs.  A regression that broadened the
      *  IS NOT NUMERIC clause (e.g., to also reject 16-digit
      *  numerics) would surface here as a failed FLG-CARDFILTER-
      *  ISVALID assertion.
      *
      *  Why '0000000000000001' is the chosen valid input
      *  ------------------------------------------------
      *  '0000000000000001' is 16 characters (matches CC-CARD-NUM
      *  PIC X(16) length), all-numeric (passes the IS NOT NUMERIC
      *  test), and non-zero when interpreted via CC-CARD-NUM-N
      *  REDEFINES (fails the EQUAL ZEROS test) -- the smallest
      *  16-digit non-zero card number satisfying the three-clause
      *  validation.  Larger valid inputs would prove the same
      *  path; the smallest is chosen for documentation clarity.
      *  This input is supplied by the test author, NOT derived
      *  from production logic.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC1 prelude:
      *    CC-CARD-NUM = '0000000000000001' (PIC X(16) literal MOVE)
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    '1'         - WS-EDIT-CARD-FLAG flipped by SET FLG-
      *                  CARDFILTER-ISVALID (production line 718;
      *                  88-level on WS-EDIT-CARD-FLAG VALUE '1' per
      *                  COCRDSLC.cbl line 61).  Test asserts the
      *                  side effect; does NOT recompute or
      *                  paraphrase the SET logic.
      *    '0000000000000001'
      *                - CDEMO-CARD-NUM populated by line 717 MOVE
      *                  CC-CARD-NUM-N TO CDEMO-CARD-NUM.  CDEMO-
      *                  CARD-NUM is PIC 9(16) per COCOM01Y; cobol-
      *                  check renders PIC 9(16) in the 16-digit
      *                  zero-padded form for EXPECT comparison.
      *    SPACES      - WS-RETURN-MSG retains BEFORE-EACH default
      *                  (matching 88-level WS-RETURN-MSG-OFF on
      *                  the LOW-VALUES VALUE per COCRDSLC.cbl line
      *                  135 -- INITIALIZE on a PIC X group fills
      *                  with SPACES which compares equal to the
      *                  88-level LOW-VALUES match in cobol-check's
      *                  EXPECT semantics).  No diagnostic message
      *                  is set on the success path -- a regression
      *                  that fired the zeros-or-non-numeric branch
      *                  would write the production literal "CARD
      *                  ID FILTER,IF SUPPLIED MUST BE A 16 DIGIT
      *                  NUMBER" here, which this assertion catches.
      *
      *  VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES asserts the production
      *  invariant that 2220-EDIT-CARD contains zero EXEC CICS
      *  verbs (a regression introducing one would inflate the
      *  count and fail the VERIFY).  Same pattern as COTRN01C
      *  TC3 / COBIL00C TC3 / COACTVWC TC1 -- pure-WS validation
      *  paragraphs.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDSLC 2220-EDIT-CARD accepts valid 16-digit num'
            MOVE '0000000000000001' TO CC-CARD-NUM
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 2220-EDIT-CARD THRU 2220-EDIT-CARD-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-EDIT-CARD-FLAG TO BE '1'
            EXPECT CDEMO-CARD-NUM TO BE '0000000000000001'
            EXPECT WS-RETURN-MSG TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED TO BE 'N'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES



      ******************************************************************
      *  TC2 -- 2220-EDIT-CARD rejects empty card number (SPACES)
      *
      *  Drives 2220-EDIT-CARD (production lines 685-723) along the
      *  EMPTY-INPUT rejection path:
      *
      *    IF CC-CARD-NUM   EQUAL LOW-VALUES              (line 691)
      *    OR CC-CARD-NUM   EQUAL SPACES                  (line 692)
      *    OR CC-CARD-NUM-N EQUAL ZEROS                   (line 693)
      *        SET INPUT-ERROR           TO TRUE          (line 694)
      *        SET FLG-CARDFILTER-BLANK  TO TRUE          (line 695)
      *        IF WS-RETURN-MSG-OFF                       (line 696)
      *           SET WS-PROMPT-FOR-CARD TO TRUE          (line 697)
      *        END-IF
      *        MOVE ZEROES       TO CDEMO-CARD-NUM        (line 700)
      *        GO TO 2220-EDIT-CARD-EXIT                  (line 701)
      *    END-IF.
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of AAP TC3 "Blank card number
      *  rejected".  Production-mandated invariant: 2200-EDIT-MAP-
      *  INPUTS (lines 622-627) MOVEs LOW-VALUES TO CC-CARD-NUM when
      *  CARDSIDI = '*' OR SPACES; testing CC-CARD-NUM = SPACES
      *  directly here proves the downstream 2220 correctly handles
      *  what 2200 hands it.  After line-701 GO TO EXIT, the IS
      *  NOT NUMERIC branch is NOT entered -- the empty-check is
      *  the FIRST gate that short-circuits before format
      *  validation.  Asserting FLG-CARDFILTER-BLANK (' ') vs FLG-
      *  CARDFILTER-NOT-OK ('0') in TC3 proves the BLANK path ran,
      *  not the format path.  Asserting WS-RETURN-MSG carries the
      *  WS-PROMPT-FOR-CARD literal "Card number not provided"
      *  proves the line-697 SET fired (WS-RETURN-MSG-OFF was TRUE
      *  at entry per BEFORE-EACH INITIALIZE WS-MISC-STORAGE).
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC2 prelude:
      *    CC-CARD-NUM = SPACES (PIC X(16) MOVE; matches line-692)
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    '1'         - WS-INPUT-FLAG flipped by line 694 SET
      *                  INPUT-ERROR (88-level VALUE '1' per
      *                  COCRDSLC.cbl line 53).  Test asserts side
      *                  effect.
      *    ' '         - WS-EDIT-CARD-FLAG flipped by line 695 SET
      *                  FLG-CARDFILTER-BLANK (88-level VALUE ' '
      *                  per COCRDSLC.cbl line 62).  KEY differential
      *                  vs TC3's '0'.
      *    'Card number not provided'
      *                - WS-RETURN-MSG flipped by line 697 SET WS-
      *                  PROMPT-FOR-CARD (88-level VALUE per
      *                  COCRDSLC.cbl lines 140-141).  Test asserts
      *                  the side effect; does NOT recompute or
      *                  paraphrase the SET logic.
      *    '0000000000000000'
      *                - CDEMO-CARD-NUM flipped by line 700 MOVE
      *                  ZEROES (PIC 9(16) zero, 16-digit padded form).
      *
      *  VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES -- same no-CICS invariant
      *  as TC1.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDSLC 2220-EDIT-CARD rejects empty card number'
            MOVE SPACES TO CC-CARD-NUM
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 2220-EDIT-CARD THRU 2220-EDIT-CARD-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-INPUT-FLAG TO BE '1'
            EXPECT WS-EDIT-CARD-FLAG TO BE ' '
            EXPECT WS-RETURN-MSG TO BE 'Card number not provided'
            EXPECT CDEMO-CARD-NUM TO BE '0000000000000000'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES



      ******************************************************************
      *  TC3 -- 2220-EDIT-CARD rejects non-numeric card number
      *
      *  Drives 2220-EDIT-CARD along the IS NOT NUMERIC rejection
      *  path -- the format-fail gate that prevents 9100-GETCARD-
      *  BYACCTCARD from being called on malformed input.  Off-
      *  platform expression of the AAP TC2 "Card not found"
      *  pathway along the format-rejection branch (the literal
      *  AAP TC2 NOTFND on CARDDAT requires the translator for
      *  EVALUATE WS-RESP-CD WHEN DFHRESP(NOTFND) on production
      *  lines 752-761; the IS NOT NUMERIC gate is the last off-
      *  platform-reachable check that has the same downstream
      *  effect of suppressing the CICS READ).
      *
      *  Production paragraph (relevant branch):
      *
      *    IF CC-CARD-NUM  IS NOT NUMERIC                 (line 706)
      *        SET INPUT-ERROR TO TRUE                    (line 707)
      *        SET FLG-CARDFILTER-NOT-OK TO TRUE          (line 708)
      *        IF WS-RETURN-MSG-OFF                       (line 709)
      *           MOVE 'CARD ID FILTER,IF SUPPLIED MUST
      *                 BE A 16 DIGIT NUMBER'
      *                                  TO WS-RETURN-MSG (line 710-2)
      *        END-IF
      *        MOVE ZERO       TO CDEMO-CARD-NUM          (line 714)
      *        GO TO 2220-EDIT-CARD-EXIT                  (line 715)
      *    END-IF.
      *
      *  Note: the line-691-693 OR-chain is FALSE for input
      *  '000000000000000A' because (a) the value is not LOW-VALUES
      *  / SPACES (CC-CARD-NUM is alphanumeric not blank) and (b)
      *  CC-CARD-NUM-N EQUAL ZEROS evaluates against a redefined
      *  PIC 9(16) view of an alphanumeric byte sequence -- under
      *  GnuCOBOL, this comparison short-circuits FALSE because
      *  the underlying bytes (X'30...30 41') are not a valid
      *  packed-decimal-zero pattern.  The IS NOT NUMERIC gate on
      *  line 706 then evaluates TRUE (the trailing 'A' is non-
      *  numeric), routing the testcase into the format-rejection
      *  handler.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions: CC-CARD-NUM = '000000000000000A' (test-
      *  author supplied: 16 chars, alphanumeric, non-blank --
      *  trips IS NOT NUMERIC TRUE on the trailing 'A' while
      *  passing the empty-OR-zero gate on line 691-693).
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    '1'         - WS-INPUT-FLAG flipped by line 707.
      *    '0'         - WS-EDIT-CARD-FLAG flipped by line 708 SET
      *                  FLG-CARDFILTER-NOT-OK (88-level VALUE '0'
      *                  per line 60).  Differential vs TC2's ' '.
      *    'CARD ID FILTER,IF SUPPLIED MUST BE A 16 DIGIT NUMBER'
      *                - WS-RETURN-MSG literal MOVE'd verbatim by
      *                  lines 710-712.  Test asserts the side
      *                  effect; does NOT recompute.  COMMA
      *                  IMMEDIATELY after "FILTER" preserved
      *                  exactly as in production (no space).
      *    '0000000000000000'
      *                - CDEMO-CARD-NUM flipped by line 714 MOVE
      *                  ZERO (PIC 9(16) zero, 16-digit padded form).
      *
      *  VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES -- same no-CICS invariant
      *  as TC1 / TC2.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDSLC 2220-EDIT-CARD rejects non-numeric card'
            MOVE '000000000000000A' TO CC-CARD-NUM
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 2220-EDIT-CARD THRU 2220-EDIT-CARD-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-INPUT-FLAG TO BE '1'
            EXPECT WS-EDIT-CARD-FLAG TO BE '0'
            EXPECT WS-RETURN-MSG TO BE
                'CARD ID FILTER,IF SUPPLIED MUST BE A 16 DIGIT NUMBER'
            EXPECT CDEMO-CARD-NUM TO BE '0000000000000000'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES



      ******************************************************************
      *  TC4 -- 2210-EDIT-ACCOUNT accepts a valid 11-digit account id
      *
      *  Drives 2210-EDIT-ACCOUNT (production lines 647-683) along
      *  the SUCCESS path that gates 9100-GETCARD-BYACCTCARD
      *  downstream as the COMPANION validation paragraph to TC1's
      *  2220-EDIT-CARD.  Production line 344 (executed inside
      *  0000-MAIN's WHEN CDEMO-PGM-ENTER AND CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM
      *  EQUAL LIT-CCLISTPGM branch) PERFORMs 9000-READ-DATA THRU
      *  9000-READ-DATA-EXIT only after BOTH 2210-EDIT-ACCOUNT and
      *  2220-EDIT-CARD validate their inputs via 2200-EDIT-MAP-
      *  INPUTS' line 630-634 chain.  Asserting BOTH validation
      *  paragraphs in sister testcases (TC1 covers 2220, TC4
      *  covers 2210) proves both arms of the gate are wired
      *  correctly.
      *
      *  The paragraph executes:
      *
      *    SET FLG-ACCTFILTER-NOT-OK TO TRUE              (line 648)
      *    IF CC-ACCT-ID = LOW-VALUES OR SPACES OR
      *       CC-ACCT-ID-N EQUAL ZEROS                    (line 651-3)
      *        ... (FALSE; '00000000001' is non-zero)
      *    IF CC-ACCT-ID IS NOT NUMERIC                   (line 665)
      *        ... (FALSE; '00000000001' is all-numeric)
      *    ELSE                                           (line 675)
      *        MOVE CC-ACCT-ID TO CDEMO-ACCT-ID           (line 676)
      *        SET FLG-ACCTFILTER-ISVALID TO TRUE         (line 677)
      *    END-IF.
      *
      *  Why '00000000001' is the chosen valid input
      *  -------------------------------------------
      *  Same selection rationale as TC1 (smallest 11-digit non-
      *  zero account id satisfying all three validation clauses).
      *  Matches the canonical input used across the testsuite
      *  family (COACTVWC TC1) for consistent traceability.  Test-
      *  author supplied; NOT derived from production logic.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC4 prelude:
      *    CC-ACCT-ID = '00000000001' (PIC X(11) literal MOVE)
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    '1'         - WS-EDIT-ACCT-FLAG flipped by SET FLG-
      *                  ACCTFILTER-ISVALID (production line 677;
      *                  88-level on WS-EDIT-ACCT-FLAG VALUE '1' per
      *                  COCRDSLC.cbl line 57).  Test asserts the
      *                  side effect; does NOT recompute the SET.
      *    '00000000001'
      *                - CDEMO-ACCT-ID populated by line 676 MOVE
      *                  CC-ACCT-ID TO CDEMO-ACCT-ID; CDEMO-ACCT-ID
      *                  is PIC 9(11) per COCOM01Y; cobol-check
      *                  renders PIC 9(11) in the 11-digit padded
      *                  form for EXPECT comparison.
      *    SPACES      - WS-RETURN-MSG retains BEFORE-EACH default
      *                  (matching 88-level WS-RETURN-MSG-OFF on
      *                  the LOW-VALUES VALUE per COCRDSLC.cbl line
      *                  135).  No diagnostic message is set on the
      *                  success path -- a regression that fired
      *                  the zeros-or-non-numeric branch would write
      *                  the production literal "ACCOUNT FILTER,IF
      *                  SUPPLIED MUST BE A 11 DIGIT NUMBER" here,
      *                  which this assertion catches.
      *
      *  VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES asserts the production
      *  invariant that 2210-EDIT-ACCOUNT contains zero EXEC CICS
      *  verbs (a regression introducing one would inflate the
      *  count and fail the VERIFY).  Same pattern as TC1 / TC2 /
      *  TC3 -- pure-WS validation paragraphs.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDSLC 2210-EDIT-ACCOUNT accepts valid 11-digit id'
            MOVE '00000000001' TO CC-ACCT-ID
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 2210-EDIT-ACCOUNT THRU 2210-EDIT-ACCOUNT-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-EDIT-ACCT-FLAG TO BE '1'
            EXPECT CDEMO-ACCT-ID TO BE '00000000001'
            EXPECT WS-RETURN-MSG TO BE SPACES
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES



      ******************************************************************
      *  TC5 -- 1100-SCREEN-INIT populates header from program literals
      *
      *  Drives 1100-SCREEN-INIT (production lines 427-455).  Pure-
      *  WS preamble called by 1000-SEND-MAP (lines 413-414) on
      *  every screen-render pass -- first entry, validation
      *  failure, data-load success, and PF3 fall-through.  Zero
      *  EXEC CICS verbs and zero PERFORM statements (only
      *  invocation seam is FUNCTION CURRENT-DATE on lines 430/437);
      *  the cleanest off-platform test target in COCRDSLC.
      *
      *  Production paragraph (assertion-relevant subset):
      *
      *    MOVE LOW-VALUES     TO CCRDSLAO                (line 428)
      *    MOVE FUNCTION CURRENT-DATE TO WS-CURDATE-DATA  (line 430)
      *    MOVE CCDA-TITLE01   TO TITLE01O OF CCRDSLAO    (line 432)
      *    MOVE CCDA-TITLE02   TO TITLE02O OF CCRDSLAO    (line 433)
      *    MOVE LIT-THISTRANID TO TRNNAMEO OF CCRDSLAO    (line 434)
      *    MOVE LIT-THISPGM    TO PGMNAMEO OF CCRDSLAO    (line 435)
      *    ... (FUNCTION CURRENT-DATE second MOVE on line 437,
      *         WS-CURDATE-MM/DD/YY and WS-CURTIME-HH/MM/SS
      *         decomposition MOVEs on lines 439-449)
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of AAP TC4 "PF3 exit" and TC5
      *  "XCTL back to list" generalised to the screen-render
      *  preamble that runs on every cycle -- including PF3
      *  fall-through which 0000-MAIN's WHEN CCARD-AID-PFK03
      *  branch (production lines 305-334) reaches via 1000-
      *  SEND-MAP THRU 1000-SEND-MAP-EXIT before issuing the
      *  EXEC CICS XCTL.  Literal AAP TC4/TC5 XCTL pathways
      *  require translator-defined EIBAID and CCARD-AID-PFK03
      *  88-level; 1100-SCREEN-INIT exercises the preamble that
      *  PRECEDES the XCTL on every cycle.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'CCDL'      - LIT-THISTRANID (production line 166 PIC
      *                  X(4) VALUE 'CCDL') MOVE'd to TRNNAMEO
      *                  by line 434.  Test asserts side effect
      *                  verbatim; does NOT recompute or paraphrase.
      *    'COCRDSLC'  - LIT-THISPGM (production line 164 PIC
      *                  X(8) VALUE 'COCRDSLC') MOVE'd to
      *                  PGMNAMEO by line 435.
      *
      *  CURDATEO / CURTIMEO are NOT asserted because they
      *  derive from FUNCTION CURRENT-DATE (non-deterministic).
      *  TITLE01O / TITLE02O are 40-byte slots whose space-
      *  padding varies; the 4-byte TRNNAMEO / 8-byte PGMNAMEO
      *  are unambiguous and are the production-literal-driven
      *  slots most tightly coupled to a regression in the line
      *  434-435 MOVE pair.
      *
      *  VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES asserts the production
      *  invariant that 1100-SCREEN-INIT contains zero EXEC CICS
      *  verbs (regression introducing one would inflate the
      *  count and fail the VERIFY).  Same pattern as TC1-TC4.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDSLC 1100-SCREEN-INIT populates header from lits'
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 1100-SCREEN-INIT
            EXPECT TRNNAMEO OF CCRDSLAO TO BE 'CCDL'
            EXPECT PGMNAMEO OF CCRDSLAO TO BE 'COCRDSLC'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  End of testsuite COCRDSLC CARD DETAIL VIEW TRANSACTION
      ******************************************************************
